This document describes overlays provided in the kernel packages
For generic Armbian overlays documentation please see
https://docs.armbian.com/Hardware_Allwinner_overlays/

### Platform:

sun55i-t527 (Allwinner A523/T527)

### Provided overlays:

- avaota-a1-disable-lcd

### Overlay details:

### avaota-a1-disable-lcd

Frees the on-board 1.14" 135x240 ST7789V SPI-LCD for the RISC-V E906
co-processor.

By default the panel is enabled in the base device tree, so Linux drives it
and exposes it as /dev/fb0 (S_SPI0, pins PL10/PL11/PL12, plus the
PL8/PL9/PL13 GPIO control lines). Adding this overlay disables the r_spi0
controller: the Linux SPI/fbtft drivers are never probed, leaving the bus and
the GPIO lines unclaimed so custom E906 bare-metal firmware can drive the
panel.

To use it, add to /boot/armbianEnv.txt:

    overlays=avaota-a1-disable-lcd

and reboot. Remove the line again to give the panel back to Linux.

Playing with the E906 (once this overlay is active):

    scp your-fw.elf avaota@<ip>:/lib/firmware/rproc-7130000.e906_rproc-fw
    echo stop  | sudo tee /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc0/state
    echo start | sudo tee /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc0/state
